   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The colors",
   "texto": [
    "Almost all basic colors are adjective in -i: **あかい** (red), **あおい** (blue), **しろい** (white), **くろい** (black), **きいろい** (yellow).",
    "They go before the name: **くろい ジャケット** (black jacket).",
    "**の** can replace a name already mentioned, such as «the» in Spanish: **あおい の** (blue), **やすい の** (cheap)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "In the store",
   "texto": [
    "**これ を ください** = I'll take this one.",
    "**もっと** = more. **もっと やすい の は あります か** (do you have a cheaper one?).",
    "**そして** joins two sentences: «and»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Compare with hd",
   "texto": [
    "**より** means «that» in the comparisons and goes behind what is compared: **A は B より やすい です** (A is cheaper than B).",
    "The **no cambia** adjective: there is no special form for «cheaper»."
   ]
